CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-007: Screwdriver Antenna — 40m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 7.000–7.300 MHz (7 points, 0.050 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 3.086 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~280)
CM    X = 864 ohm    (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 40m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 40m is the classic low-band mobile workhorse.
CM  Quarter-wave at 7.15 MHz = 10.49m; whip is 22.9% of QW.
CM  Heavy loading; efficiency is 4-7 dBd below full-size antenna.
CM  Radiation resistance drops to ~3-5 ohm; loss resistance
CM  from coil (3.086 ohm) approaches Rrad. Radial system is
CM  critical — maintain good contact and radial length.
CM  Sweep covers full 40m band: 7.000-7.300 MHz.
CM ============================================================
CE
GW 1  20  0 0 0       0 0 2.4     0.006
GW 2   4  0 0 0.005   2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 3   4  0 0 0.005  -2.4 0 0.005  0.006
GW 4   4  0 0 0.005   0 2.4 0.005  0.006
GW 5   4  0 0 0.005   0 -2.4 0.005 0.006
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
LD 0  1  1  1  3.086  864
EX 0  1  1  0  1  0
FR 0  7  0  0  7.000  0.050
RP 0  37  73  1000  0  0  5  5
EN
